        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: City of Palms Park, Fort Myers, Florida\n- People: Mike Greenwell\n- Organizations: Boston Red Sox, National Club Baseball Association\n- Events: 2008 NCBA Division I World Series\n- Topics: baseball, spring training, concerts\n\nFacts:\n- Mike Greenwell was born on July 18, 1963.\n- Mike Greenwell was a former Major League Baseball left fielder who played his entire MLB career with the Boston Red Sox from 1985 to 1996.\n- City of Palms Park is a stadium in Fort Myers, Florida that is primarily used for baseball and is also occasionally used by the City of Fort Myers for concerts.\n- Mike Greenwell, who is from Fort Myers, was instrumental in bringing the Boston Red Sox to the city for spring training.\n- The 2008 National Club Baseball Association Division I World Series was played at City of Palms Park in Fort Myers, Florida from May 23 to May 29, 2008.",
